---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import { appConfig } from '../../../app.config'

const description = 'What this SaaS template stores. The only database row is operational, not personal.'
const canonical = new URL('/privacy', appConfig.app.url).href
---

<Base title={`Privacy · ${appConfig.app.name}`} description={description} canonical={canonical}>
  <main id="content" class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Public pages are static HTML. They do not read the database and they do not set cookies.
    </p>
    <h2>What is stored</h2>
    <p>
      The database has one table, app_meta. It holds a schema version so the template can show that
      migrations ran. That row is operational data, not information about a person. The read-only
      API can return the application name and the list of enabled plugins.
    </p>
    <h2>The application shell</h2>
    <p>
      <a href="/app">/app</a> does not sign anyone in. Requests that would change data are refused.
      This site has no account.
    </p>
    <p>
      The <a href="/terms">terms</a> match this site as published. A later change that starts keeping
      personal information has to rewrite this page in the same change, including what is kept, how
      long it is kept, and how it is deleted.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
